# The git pre-commit hook is a bash script: force LF so a Windows checkout never
# materializes it with CRLF (a CRLF shebang can break execution via git's hook
# runner). core.hooksPath points git at hooks/ (see CLAUDE.md "Linting").
hooks/pre-commit text eol=lf

# Same reason, every bash script: with core.autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows
# default) a Windows checkout materializes these with CRLF, and bash then dies
# on the stray \r at the end of every line. That would break the Windows CI job
# running tests/test-install.sh, and it is also what makes shellcheck report
# SC1017 on every line of a Windows working tree.
*.sh text eol=lf
